Heavy Periods and Skin Comfort: How to Reduce Everyday Irritation

During your period, your skin may be exposed to moisture, friction, and prolonged contact with a sanitary pad. If your flow is heavy, you may spend more time using menstrual products, making comfort particularly important.

Why Can Skin Feel Uncomfortable During Periods?

Several factors can contribute to discomfort, including moisture, friction, heat, prolonged use of a damp pad, and sensitivity to certain materials or fragrances.

Everyone's skin reacts differently.

How Can You Improve Period Comfort?
Change Your Pad Regularly

Avoid keeping a saturated pad on for longer than necessary.

Keep the Area Dry

Good hygiene and regular changes can help reduce prolonged moisture.

Choose Comfortable Underwear

Soft, breathable underwear can improve overall comfort.

Avoid Products That Irritate Your Skin

If a fragranced product causes irritation, stop using it and consider a gentler alternative.

Choose a Comfortable Pad

The surface and fit of a sanitary pad matter, especially during heavy-flow days.

